{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, five failed local password login attempts lock the account, while four failures do not.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active policy sets deny=5. Direct PAM login testing showed successful authentication after four failures, five recorded failures after the fifth attempt, and denial of the correct password while locked. The boundary behavior was repeated successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a75bf660b1f943e7","cmd-715cb73cc5cd4209","cmd-fc6949d330234954","cmd-8ad12ed39eac4505"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The account lock lasts five minutes and then automatically permits password login again.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active policy sets unlock_time=300. A timed test directly showed immediate denial while locked followed by successful authentication 307 seconds after lock confirmation, with the failure ledger cleared afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a75bf660b1f943e7","cmd-e8b5ac4be9654d2d","cmd-8ad12ed39eac4505"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The policy edit and retained rollback copy had a clear configuration-safety role. Temporary PAM helpers, accounts, credentials, and faillock records were bounded validation prerequisites and were cleaned up. The mandatory reboot was preceded by cleanup. Final evidence shows no probe accounts or validation path, no failed units, healthy package state, and no new listening exposure; lifecycle socket and temporary-file differences are normal reboot PID/boot-ID churn.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a75bf660b1f943e7","cmd-367d9f8629da474c","cmd-b2871082c5674bc3","cmd-715cb73cc5cd4209","cmd-edef3a3884a24651","cmd-e8b5ac4be9654d2d","cmd-5e62b6b4a4d546cc","cmd-92858cec8cd9487b","cmd-c3673231752e45aa","cmd-fc6949d330234954","cmd-8ad12ed39eac4505","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied by direct configuration and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it records a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement and connection interruption, a different post-restart identity, preserved configuration hash, healthy system state, and recovered lockout behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["The timed test sampled the locked state immediately and recovery at 307 seconds, but did not behaviorally sample immediately before or exactly at 300 seconds; the exact boundary is therefore supported partly by the observed unlock_time=300 configuration.","Lifecycle snapshots are bounded and do not inventory PAM configuration or local accounts; those final-state checks rely on the captured executor commands."]}
